RK3588 DW HDMI QP audio packet diagnostics
===========================================

This directory contains local hardware test tooling.  It is not a kernel
selftest and the audio_debug_* sysfs files are not a stable userspace ABI.

Scope
-----

The tests use ordinary S32_LE LPCM through the HDMI hardware PCM.  They do
not test IEC 61937, DTS-HD, TrueHD, MAT, or userspace IEC958 conversion.
Keep the display active while testing; the driver rejects diagnostic MMIO
reads when the HDMI link is disabled.

Run the complete matrix as root:

  tools/testing/rk3588-hdmi-audio-debug/run.sh matrix

Run only the five automatic-mode baselines:

  tools/testing/rk3588-hdmi-audio-debug/run.sh baseline

Run one case, optionally selecting Layout and Sample_Present modes:

  tools/testing/rk3588-hdmi-audio-debug/run.sh run 4ch-96k 1 0x0003

The optional arguments after FORMAT select a Rockchip TX FIFO threshold and
DMA maxburst for the next stream.  The threshold accepts "auto" or 1 through
31, while maxburst accepts 1 through 16.  For example, test 4-channel 96 kHz
LPCM with threshold 28 and maxburst 8:

  tools/testing/rk3588-hdmi-audio-debug/run.sh fifo 4ch-96k 28 8

In automatic mode RK3588 retains threshold 16 for rates through 48 kHz and
for stereo through 96 kHz.  Stereo above 96 kHz uses 24, and multichannel
above 48 kHz uses 28.  Maxburst remains 8.  The selected override mode and
effective threshold are captured in every timed snapshot.

Restore both controls without starting a stream:

  tools/testing/rk3588-hdmi-audio-debug/run.sh restore

The result root defaults to a timestamped directory below the current
directory.  Set RK3588_HDMI_AUDIO_RESULTS to place it elsewhere, and set
RK3588_HDMI_AUDIO_DURATION to change the default eight-second case duration.

Matrix
------

The baseline runs these cases with HDMI packet controls and the RK3588 TX
FIFO threshold in automatic mode:

  case       channels  rate       automatic threshold
  8ch-48k       8       48000             16
  2ch-96k       2       96000             16
  4ch-96k       4       96000             28
  8ch-96k       8       96000             28
  2ch-192k      2      192000             24

All five combinations have played cleanly with those thresholds on the
ROCK 5B+ test system.  With a fixed threshold of 16, the last three were
historically corrupt.  Threshold 28 is unsafe for a two-channel carrier: it
made both PCM and DTS consume data too quickly, while DTS was clean again at
16 and 2-channel 192 kHz PCM was clean at 24.

For each historically broken case, matrix additionally runs:

  case       layout only  Sample_Present only  both
  4ch-96k       1              0x0003           1 / 0x0003
  8ch-96k       1              0x000f           1 / 0x000f
  2ch-192k      0              0x000f           0 / 0x000f

HDMI defines Layout 0 for a stereo pair sampled up to four times in one
Audio Sample Packet, and Layout 1 for up to four channel pairs sampled once.
The four low Sample_Present bits correspond to the packet's four subpackets.
Consequently, 0x3 selects the first two Layout 1 channel pairs, while 0xf
selects all four Layout 1 pairs or all four Layout 0 temporal samples.  The
RK3588 TRM also says that non-3D audio uses no bits above this low nibble.

These combinations are structurally valid HDMI packet descriptions, but
forcing them continuously is still a test hypothesis.  No public RK3588 QP
implementation was found that programs these override fields, and automatic
Sample_Present may vary with packet cadence.  Do not treat the values as a
permanent policy without hardware results.

Captured state
--------------

After speaker-test reaches ALSA RUNNING, each case captures state at about
100 ms, 300 ms, one second, and three seconds.  Every snapshot contains:

* ALSA hw_params and runtime status;
* DW HDMI QP audio interface, packetizer, ACR, packet scheduler, clock
  monitor, and AVP error state;
* configured Layout and Sample_Present controls;
* Rockchip I2S threshold override and effective threshold;
* Rockchip I2S runtime-PM state and relevant kernel messages.

The script clears only the documented audio error bits immediately before
starting each stream.  The status output decodes them as follows:

  invalid_sample_present
    The packetizer rejected the Sample_Present configuration.  If this
    appears only with an override, reject that mask.

  fifo_underflow
    The QP audio-interface FIFO ran out of input data.

  fifo_overflow
    The QP audio-interface FIFO received data faster than it drained.

  i2s_ws
    The QP detected an I2S word-select protocol error.

  i2s_bbit
    The QP detected disparity between received IEC60958 B bits.

If corruption occurs while all five remain clear, these detectors do not
support a FIFO starvation or I2S framing explanation.  Compare automatic and
forced packetizer state next; do not infer that a forced combination is
correct merely because the AVR remains locked.
